{"text": " Every hour you spend building a prompt library saves 10 hours in the future. The best professionals do not start from scratch, they remix. In this lesson, how to structure a reusable prompt library, categories, variables, version control and team access. We build a template system with placeholders that works for any team size. A prompt library is a structured collection of tested, reusable prompts organized by use case. The difference between a prompt library and a folder of text files is versioning, testing and organization. A professional prompt library treats prompts code. Each has a purpose, a version history, performance notes and is stored where your team can access and improve it. A prompt library compounds in value over time. Every tested prompt is institutional knowledge. Every performance note prevents a colleague from making the same mistake. Remember this, every time you develop a prompt that works reliably, add it to the library immediately. The effort of capture is trivial compared to the effort of rediscovering it. Apply what you learn in this lesson and you will see results immediately. Your skills bear fruit.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.92, "text": " Every hour you spend building a prompt library saves 10 hours in the future.", "tokens": [50364, 2048, 1773, 291, 3496, 2390, 257, 12391, 6405, 19155, 1266, 2496, 294, 264, 2027, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16882319948566493, "compression_ratio": 1.517766497461929, "no_speech_prob": 0.005310464184731245, "words": [{"word": " Every", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.5, "probability": 0.7644047737121582}, {"word": " hour", "start": 0.5, "end": 0.94, "probability": 0.9974731802940369}, {"word": " you", "start": 0.94, "end": 1.16, "probability": 0.9915800094604492}, {"word": " spend", "start": 1.16, "end": 1.46, "probability": 0.9971755743026733}, {"word": " building", "start": 1.46, "end": 1.98, "probability": 0.9957671165466309}, {"word": " a", "start